### Normalized scores (1–100)

> Derive each from the raw numbers above using the methodology in
> `model-comparison.md`. Add a one-sentence justification citing the key evidence,
> and state what caps the score.
>
> **OVERALL SCORE FORMULA (v4, see `RULES.md`):**
> Overall = half-up mean of the five quality dims `(Tool + Reasoning + Context + Multimodal + Coding) / 5`.
> **NEVER include Cost efficiency** — scored independently.

- **Tool use: 93/100.** Exceptional performance across multiple coding benchmarks including FrontierCode 2.0 (49.1%), FrontierSWE v2 (69.9%), and OSWorld 2.1 (89.3%), demonstrating top-tier capabilities in complex software engineering tasks.
- **Reasoning: 92/100.** Strong performance on scientific reasoning benchmarks like Terminal-Bench-Science (74.6%), Humanity's Last Exam (74.2%), and Chartography (73.4%), indicating advanced analytical capabilities across domains.
- **Context window: 96/100.** 1M token context window places it in the highest tier for handling long-form tasks and complex workflows.
- **Multimodal: 83/100.** Text and image input capabilities with strong performance on vision-based tasks as demonstrated in official benchmarks.
- **Coding: 95/100.** Outstanding performance in coding benchmarks including SWE-bench equivalent (FrontierSWE v2: 69.9%), automation tasks (AutomationBench: 51.4%), and computer use (OSWorld 2.1: 89.3%).
- **Cost efficiency: 42/100.** Premium pricing at $8/$40 per MTok input/output makes it one of the more expensive models on the market, though slightly more affordable than its predecessor.
- **Overall Score: 91.8/100.** Mean of the five quality dimensions (Tool, Reasoning, Context, Multimodal, Coding), reflecting exceptional performance across all domains with particular strength in technical and scientific tasks.

